# Sprint 2 Review and Retrospective

## What was completed 
By the end of Sprint 2 the team developed the final functional and user focused improved prototype. The main features in it includes appointment booking, cancellation and rescheduling hence allowing students to view all the available appointment slots and book their clinic visits online. Other main features include allowing clinic staff to manage appointments as required and admins to manage users to keep an organized system.


## What went well 
During the development stage the team was able to transfer the earlier design contents and the wireframes into a functional prototype. Also implementing the main features helped show how the clinic appointment system would work in a real environment. 

## What needs improvement  
What needed improvement is more communication for the whole work to be able to flow together more smoothly and effectively.

## Final outcome 
The project was successfully produced into a functional user focused improved prototype of the clinic appointment system. It has also showed how digital appointment management can improve healthcare services for university students hence directly contributing to the original goal SDG 3 .





